// Shared, framework-neutral message for the HIL 3-way QoS-matrix comparison
// (rmw_tickle/comparison.md's "Planned: HIL 3-way QoS-matrix comparison" section).
//
// One canonical message for all 9 scenarios, deliberately small and fixed-size: this exercise is
// about protocol/QoS-handling overhead (RELIABILITY/DURABILITY/HISTORY/DEADLINE/LIVELINESS/
// LIFESPAN), not payload-size effects - those are already covered by the existing rmw-layer
// Array1k/Struct16 comparison (comparison.md's own "Performance comparison" section, above).
//
// Both fastddsgen and CycloneDDS's own idlc compile this exact file - "identical data" is a
// byte-identical source guarantee, not a hand-matched one (comparison.md's own design note).
//
// @extensibility(FINAL) pinned explicitly, not left to whatever each tool's own current default
// happens to be (idlc warns this may change to "appendable" in a future release) - both vendors
// must interpret this identically regardless of tool version.
@extensibility(FINAL)
struct Bench {
    unsigned long seq;          // per-Publisher monotonic sample counter, starts at 1
    unsigned long long send_ns; // sender's own monotonic send timestamp (CLOCK_MONOTONIC, ns)
    octet payload[64];          // fixed filler, unused by any scenario's own logic
};
